  "appearance": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "The finished Gu looks like a beetle with two sharp ends and a fat middle, about the size of a young man’s fist. It is like blue jade, soft and cool to the touch, with a golden eye on its plump back that flashes with lightning. Fang Yuan’s semi-finished copy has a vague pottery look with no hint of life: grey stone carved into a beetle shape with a big belly, sharp head and tail, and no antennas or legs.",
        "chapters": [
          487
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "appearance",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Second Aperture Gu is not a mortal Gu but a rank six Immortal Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          377
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_mortal_gu",
          "sys_immortal_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The San Cha revelation chapters do not describe a finished Gu worm body.",
        "chapters": [],
        "certainty": "inferred",
        "confidence": "C",
        "verification": "no_citation",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_worms"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "To refine it at San Cha Mountain, apertures are the main ingredient. Fang Yuan uses beast strength placenta Gu to devour Gu Master apertures and raise the future Second Aperture Gu’s aptitude; after Tie Mu Bai’s rank five peak stage aperture is absorbed, that aptitude reaches forty percent.",
        "chapters": [
          379
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_beast_strength_placenta_gu",
          "sys_gu_master",
          "char_tie_mu_bai"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "visual_confidence": "text_described"
  },
  "abilities": {
    "activation_raw": null,
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan’s own accounting at first revelation is that with A grade ninety percent aptitude, a second aperture would mean a hundred and eighty percent primeval essence, double primeval essence recovery speed, and a second set of Gu worms, sharply raising battle strength among the same rank.",
        "chapters": [
          377
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
  "feeding": {
    "known": false,
    "food_raw": null,
    "foods": [],
    "claims": []
  },
  "refinement": {
    "recipes": [
      "rcp_second_aperture_gu_recipe"
    ],
    "used_in_recipes": [],
    "refinement_materials": [],
    "confirmed_evolutions": [],
    "related_variants": [],
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "The blessed land’s original master was a strength path Gu Immortal who created the recipe and died in a tribulation before the crucial step. That final obsession became land spirit Ba Gui, and the dying wish that tests a new owner is to refine Second Aperture Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          377
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "recipe-at-san-cha-mountain",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_immortal"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In Fang Yuan’s previous-life knowledge the legendary Gu became extinct before the first one was created. The first prior attempt fails when the chosen strength path Gu Master is poor at refining and dies after starting the process. Later attempts come too late: immortal essence is severely lacking, the land spirit is weakened, Gu Masters kill the refining strength path Gu Master and then the land spirit, and with immortal essence expended the refinement ends in utter failure.",
        "chapters": [
          377
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "recipe-at-san-cha-mountain",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_gu_masters"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Refining it consumes large immortal essence, the recipe has up to a thousand steps, and the final stage needs another rank six Immortal Gu. Fang Yuan treats the finished Gu as his greatest reward for the trip even if the blessed land itself cannot be saved afterward.",
        "chapters": [
          378
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "recipe-at-san-cha-mountain",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
