  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Land spirit Ba Gui is stunned that Fang Yuan already knows the target Gu when they speak inside the San Cha Mountain blessed land hall.",
        "chapters": [
          377
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_land_spirit",
          "char_ba_gui",
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "loc_san_cha_mountain"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Lang Ya land spirit hands Fang Yuan a finished Second Aperture Gu after a refinement Fang Yuan forced through an old agreement. That copy looks like a beetle with two sharp ends and a fat middle, about the size of a young man’s fist, blue jade to the touch, with a golden eye on its back. The Gu is already Fang Yuan’s object, but as a mortal without green grape immortal essence he cannot activate it alone. Second Aperture Gu is also an expendable Gu that disappears after use, and it cannot create a third aperture.",
        "chapters": [
          487
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "acquiring-and-activating-a-copy",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_lang_ya_land_spirit"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan also shows Lang Ya land spirit the semi-finished Second Aperture Gu he had refined himself. That product has a vague look like unfinished pottery, with no hint of life: grey stone carved into a beetle shape, big belly, sharp head and tail, and no antennas or legs. Its outline resembles the real Gu, but the quality is not comparable.",
        "chapters": [
          487
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "acquiring-and-activating-a-copy",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Later, Lang Ya land spirit pours immortal essence into the Gu and throws it into Fang Yuan. It becomes a bean-sized green light, is rejected by his first aperture at the navel, hops to his chest, and explodes into a new aperture that looks both real and virtual.",
        "chapters": [
          490
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "acquiring-and-activating-a-copy",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Ba Shi Ba holds a rank one mortal Second Aperture Gu that matches the earlier beetle form: two sharp ends, fat midsection, young-man’s-fist size, blue jade feel, golden eye on the back. Fang Yuan tells Xia Cha he modified the original Immortal Gu into a series from rank one to six, and that he is only selling rank one copies.",
        "chapters": [
          1852
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "mortal-rank-one-variant",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_ba_shi_ba",
          "char_xia_cha"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "That mortal Gu needs neither primeval essence nor immortal essence to activate. The user drips blood onto it and feeds it until it is full; it then self-detonates and takes effect, creating a tiny rank one aperture.",
        "chapters": [
          1852
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "mortal-rank-one-variant",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
